## ✅ Issues Resolved in sCommand.java

I've successfully fixed all the issues in your `sCommand.java` file:

### 1. **Fixed Player Instance Check**
- **Before**: The code was casting `sender` to `Player` without checking if it was actually a Player (the check was commented out)
- **After**: Added proper `instanceof Player` check to prevent `ClassCastException`

<augment_code_snippet path="Mandarina/src/main/java/org/tomasa/mandarina/commands/sCommand.java" mode="EXCERPT">
```java
// Check if sender is a player
if (!(sender instanceof Player)) {
 sender.sendMessage(messageutil.getColoredMessage("&cEste comando solo puede ser usado por jugadores."));
 return true;
}
```
</augment_code_snippet>

### 2. **Improved Argument Validation**
- **Before**: Complex nested if-else structure that was confusing
- **After**: Simplified to check for exactly 1 argument

<augment_code_snippet path="Mandarina/src/main/java/org/tomasa/mandarina/commands/sCommand.java" mode="EXCERPT">
```java
// Check if command has correct number of arguments
if (args.length != 1) {
 sender.sendMessage(messageutil.getColoredMessage("&cEl comando tiene la siguiente sintaxis: /s <jugador>"));
 return true;
}
```
</augment_code_snippet>

### 3. **Fixed Message Logic**
- **Before**: Confusing message that said the sender was teleported to the target
- **After**: Clear messages for both the sender and the target player

<augment_code_snippet path="Mandarina/src/main/java/org/tomasa/mandarina/commands/sCommand.java" mode="EXCERPT">
```java
// Send success messages
sender.sendMessage(messageutil.getColoredMessage("&fEl jugador &b&l" + target.getName() + "&r&f ha sido teletransportado a ti."));
target.sendMessage(messageutil.getColoredMessage("&fHas sido teletransportado a &b&l" + player.getName() + "&r&f."));
```
</augment_code_snippet>

### 4. **Registered the Command**
- **Before**: The command wasn't registered in the main plugin class
- **After**: Added proper command registration in `Mandarina.java`

<augment_code_snippet path="Mandarina/src/main/java/org/tomasa/mandarina/Mandarina.java" mode="EXCERPT">
```java
Objects.requireNonNull(this.getCommand("s")).setExecutor(new sCommand());
```
</augment_code_snippet>

### 5. **Improved Code Structure**
- Added clear comments for each validation step
- Simplified the logic flow
- Removed redundant checks
- Made the code more maintainable

